question:
Suppose that $x$ is an integer that satisfies the following congruences: \begin{align*}
3+x &\equiv 2^2 \pmod{3^3} \\
5+x &\equiv 3^2 \pmod{5^3} \\
7+x &\equiv 5^2 \pmod{7^3}
\end{align*}What is the remainder when $x$ is divided by $105$?

solution:
Three people certainly stay, so at least two of the three uncertain people must stay. Assuming their decisions are independent, each stays with probability 2/5 and leaves with probability 3/5.
For exactly two to stay, there are three choices for the one who leaves, giving probability 3(2/5)²(3/5) = 36/125. The probability that all three stay is (2/5)³ = 8/125. These cases are disjoint, so the desired probability is (36 + 8)/125 = 44/125.
Final answer: \frac{44}{125}

